<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bathsheba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bathsheba was the wife of Uriah the Hittite who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, became the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> after he committed adultery with her and arranged Uriah's death in battle. She was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> and, with the prophet Nathan, secured his succession to the throne against his elder half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adonijah">Adonijah</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bathsheba.jpg" alt="Bathsheba" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem Drost · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Willem_Drost_-_Batsheba_met_de_brief_van_koning_David.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
